%% Streamed assistant reply lifecycle in design_paced (StreamTail.tla).
%% Combines row presentation (committed rows + repaired provisional tail) with
%% word-paced reveal across frames and the language-gate preview.
%% design_paced breaks no rule: check.sh finds every invariant true.
stateDiagram-v2
    state "Staging text in tail only (language check pending)" as Staging
    state "Backlog revealing smoothly across frames" as Pacing
    state "Screen caught up (no queued steps)" as CaughtUp
    state "Turn finished, every word committed" as Finished
    state "Language rejected, tail cleared" as Rejected
    state "Turn cancelled, queue dropped" as Cancelled

    [*] --> Staging : reply starts under language check
    [*] --> Pacing : first chunk arrives without language check
    Staging --> Staging : chunk arrives, or paced slice reveals into tail
    Staging --> CaughtUp : language check accepts with queue empty
    Staging --> Pacing : language check accepts while steps remain queued
    Staging --> Rejected : language check rejects (nothing committed)
    Staging --> Cancelled : you cancel (staged tail cleared)
    Pacing --> Pacing : chunk arrives, or paced slice reveals part of queue
    Pacing --> CaughtUp : final queued slice reveals (queue empty)
    CaughtUp --> Pacing : next chunk arrives
    CaughtUp --> CaughtUp : block boundary passes, or old row scrolls up
    CaughtUp --> Finished : reply ends and final rows commit
    Pacing --> Cancelled : you cancel (unrevealed steps dropped)
    CaughtUp --> Cancelled : you cancel
    Finished --> [*]
    Rejected --> [*]
    Cancelled --> [*]

    note right of Pacing : Each reveal takes max(ceil(backlog / window), expired steps) and applies only the k-th step's tail
    note right of CaughtUp : Block boundaries and turn Finish wait until the queue is empty

